<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Wheat sales remain slow.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Wheat sales remain slow.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hard red winter wheat cash sales remained light during the weekend and Monday, with small amounts of wheat being sold out of commercial storage, High Plains grain dealers said.</p>
<p>Some dealers speculated more sales may occur when on-farm storage is needed for fall-harvested crops.</p>
<p>Weekend rain aided Kansas and Oklahoma sorghum and should provide needed soil moisture for winter wheat planting next month.</p>
<p>The sorghum was developing well and harvest should begin late this month in Oklahoma and mid-September in Kansas.  </p>
